Spawned `ComprehensionReader`.

Result: yes, it understood the deck from slides alone.

Its inferred story matched the intended chain:
- sync encode borrows `&mut EncodeBuf`, completes bytes, then Tonic frames;
- async encode can `Pending`, so borrowed futures cannot be stored;
- Tonic stores one owned `T::Encode: Send + 'static` future;
- `EncodeBuffer` moves into the future and returns on `Ready`;
- Prost tracks field/index/phase/payload resume state;
- DSA/IAX makes ownership physical because hardware may hold raw src/dst pointers while pending.

No required fixes reported.

Optional clarifications it suggested:
- Slide 3: explicitly say Tonic stores the future after `encode` returns.
- Slide 6: reword drop-order note as cleanup before item/buffer free.
- Slide 9: define DSA/IAX as hardware copy engine holding raw src/dst pointers while pending.

